Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER
Task name: /root
Sender: /root/review_logic_error
Payload:
Found two `incomplete_integration_with_existing_code` issues:

1. Severity 5, confidence 0.99 — `convex/integrations.ts`

```ts
    if (foliosRow) {
      await ctx.db.patch(foliosRow._id, { folios, updatedAt: now });
    } else {
      await ctx.db.insert("folios", {
        userId: args.userId,
        folios,
        updatedAt: now,
      });
    }
```

The integration API writes directly to Convex, but the browser only runs `pullAll` when the authenticated user changes. Its normal sync path later replaces server folios, content, and bibliography wholesale from IndexedDB. Consequently, CLI/MCP changes are not reflected in an already-open app and can be overwritten by the browser’s next dirty-state push. The integration must participate in the existing reconciliation mechanism through reactive remote updates, version checks, or merge-aware writes.

2. Severity 3, confidence 0.98 — `packages/twyne-tools/src/archive.ts`

```ts
export function htmlToMarkdown(html: string): string {
  return decodeHtml(
    html
      .replace(/<style[\s\S]*?<\/style>/gi, "")
      .replace(/<script[\s\S]*?<\/script>/gi, "")
      .replace(/<h([1-6])[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/h\1>/gi, (_match, level, body) =>
        `${"#".repeat(Number(level))} ${stripHtml(body)}\n\n`,
      )
      .replace(/<a\b[^>]*href=["']([^"']+)["'][^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/a>/gi, (_match, href, body) =>
        `[${stripHtml(body)}](${href})`,
      )
      .replace(/<(strong|b)[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/\1>/gi, "**$2**")
      .replace(/<(em|i)[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/\1>/gi, "*$2*")
      .replace(/<code[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/code>/gi, "`$1`")
      .replace(/<li[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/li>/gi, (_match, body) => `- ${stripHtml(body)}\n`)
      .replace(/<br\s*\/?\s*>/gi, "\n")
      .replace(/<\/(p|blockquote|pre|div)>/gi, "\n\n")
      .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "")
      .replace(/[ \t]+\n/g, "\n")
      .replace(/\n{3,}/g, "\n\n")
      .trim(),
  );
}
```

The tools package reimplements HTML-to-Markdown instead of sharing or extracting Twyne’s established converter in `src/utils/html-to-markdown.ts`. The replacement loses supported manuscript semantics including ordered and nested lists, tables, task lists, strikethrough, images, math, and nested inline marks. CLI folio exports therefore differ materially from the application’s existing export contract.

